    "content": "David Barrett is the singer, songwriter, and composer behind \"One Shining Moment,\" the iconic anthem for the NCAA March Madness tournament. He wrote and recorded the original version in 1986. While Barrett sang the original, other notable artists like Luther Vandross and Teddy Pendergrass have performed versions used in the tournament. Luther Vandross Teddy Pendergrass Key Details about the Song and Singer: Original Creator: David Barrett composed and performed the original 1986 recording. Inspiration: Barrett was inspired by watching Larry Bird on TV at a bar in East Lansing, Michigan, in 1986. Tournament Usage: Since the 1987 NCAA Championship, it has been the traditional song played at the end of the final game's highlight reel. Other Versions: Luther Vandross's version is a well-known staple in the tournament's history. Alternative Performers: Teddy Pendergrass also recorded a version of the song used in the 1994 tournament. The song has become an essential part of the NCAA championship experience, often highlighting the \"poetry\" of basketball and the thrill of victory.",
